
Potential Surface Scanning

One can obtain the energy of a system as one variable
(bond length, angle, or dihedral) is systematically varied
using the scripts in this directory. For dihedral angle variation,
please see the dihdrive test job.

Please see the directions in the cmd or bat files for specification
of the desired variable, size of increments between energy evaluations, 
and total number of energy evaluations. A full optimization is executed at
each point. 

The input Z-matrix needs to be called scanzmat
except scanGB and scanPDGGB use GBzmat.

To obtain a potential of mean force for separating AcO- and MeNH3+ with GB/SA hydration:
scanGB (Windows)
csh scanGB (Linux)
See the output in scansum and scanout.

Scanning is particularly useful for finding transition structures. An example
is provided for an SN2 reaction in scanzmat. For fixed bond lengths for
atom 4 (r4), scanning of the bond length for atom five (r5) is requested in the
scanPDG- command file. Execute via
scanPDG- (Windows)
csh scanPDG- (Linux)
This example must be run with scanPDG- since it requires QM calculations for an anion.
In subsequent runs, increment r4 in scanzmat and resubmit. The results
can be tabulated in an array using Excel, which can then provide a nice plot
of the energy surface.
